1. SCOPE

This software, its source code, documentation and all constituent elements
(the "Software") are the exclusive property of Romain Guillon (the "Author").

The Software is published as source-available for the sole purpose of
demonstrating the Author's technical skills. It is NOT free software or open
source software within the meaning of the Free Software Foundation or Open
Source Initiative definitions.

2. RIGHTS GRANTED

The Author grants any person accessing the Software a free, non-exclusive,
non-transferable and revocable right to:

  a) view and read the source code for evaluation, assessment of the Author's
     skills, or personal learning;

  b) run the Software, as is and unmodified, for strictly personal, trial or
     evaluation purposes;

  c) use instances of the Software deployed online by the Author, under the
     terms of use he defines.

3. RIGHTS EXPRESSLY NOT GRANTED

Without the Author's prior written permission, the following are prohibited:

  a) reproducing, copying or extracting all or part of the source code,
     including fragments, algorithms, data structures, configuration files or
     prompt contents;

  b) modifying, adapting, translating, refactoring or creating any derivative
     work;

  c) distributing, republishing, making available, selling, renting,
     sublicensing or transferring the Software in any form or medium;

  d) any commercial, professional or organisation-internal use, including
     integration into a product, service, client deliverable or production
     infrastructure;

  e) operating the Software as part of an online service, SaaS offering or
     paid engagement for a third party;

  f) removing, altering or obscuring copyright notices, file headers or this
     license file;

  g) using the Software, in whole or in part, for training, fine-tuning,
     evaluating or feeding any machine learning model or artificial
     intelligence system, or scraping it for such purposes.

The hosting platform's fork facility is governed by that platform's terms of
service; it conveys no rights under this license and waives none of the above
prohibitions.

4. COMMERCIAL LICENSE

Any use beyond Section 2 may be granted under a separate commercial license.
Enquiries should be directed to the Author; contact details are in NOTICE.md.

5. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

This license transfers no ownership. The Author retains all economic and moral
rights in the Software. No rights are granted in the Author's trademarks,
trade names, logos or distinctive signs.

6. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Third-party libraries and components used by the Software remain governed by
their respective licenses, listed where applicable in the project's dependency
files. This license applies only to original material created by the Author.

7. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED
BY LAW, THE AUTHOR SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT OR INDIRECT DAMAGES
ARISING FROM USE OF THE SOFTWARE.

8. TERMINATION

Any breach terminates the rights granted in Section 2 automatically and
immediately, without prejudice to any action the Author may bring. The Author
